{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the manual `target += log_sum_exp(...)` marginalized categorical likelihood with a deterministic per-observation probability vector `y_prob[n] = sum_k local_weight[doc[n], k] * atom[k]` followed by the built-in observation statement `y ~ categorical(y_prob)`. This preserves the same likelihood because `categorical_lpmf(y[n] | y_prob[n])` equals the original log-sum over latent components. Also vectorized the Dirichlet priors for `local_weight` and `atom` so each top-level parameter is sampled exactly once and no prior sampling statement is inside a loop. No data fields were added or changed.
","model_safe_stan":"// ForestDB translation: Hierarchical Dirichlet Process
data {
  int<lower=1> D;
  int<lower=1> K;
  int<lower=1> V;
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=D> doc;
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=V> y;
}
parameters {
  simplex[K] global_weight;
  array[D] simplex[K] local_weight;
  array[K] simplex[V] atom;
}
model {
  array[N] vector[V] y_prob;

  global_weight ~ dirichlet(rep_vector(1.0, K));
  local_weight ~ dirichlet(5 * global_weight);
  atom ~ dirichlet(rep_vector(1.0, V));

  for (n in 1:N) {
    y_prob[n] = rep_vector(0.0, V);
    for (k in 1:K) {
      y_prob[n] += local_weight[doc[n], k] * atom[k];
    }
  }
  y ~ categorical(y_prob);
}
generated quantities {
  array[D] int<lower=1, upper=K> group_cluster;
  for (d in 1:D) {
    group_cluster[d] = categorical_rng(local_weight[d]);
  }
}
","data_safe_json":"{"D":3,"K":3,"N":5,"V":2,"doc":[3,1,1,3,2],"y":[2,2,2,2,2]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
